WEBVTT

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:31.643
You can actually become more difficult
to be around, in fact, for others,

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:34.036
and that can isolate you even further.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.761
And the real question then becomes:

00:05:35.785 --> 00:05:39.431
How do we break out of that negative
downward spiral of loneliness?

00:05:39.455 --> 00:05:41.226
(Music)

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:43.356
AG: In the US, even before the pandemic,

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:46.416
three out of four people
reported feeling lonely.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:49.046
And since we spend so much
of our time on our jobs,

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.571
work is one of the major
sources of loneliness.

00:05:52.457 --> 00:05:53.976
You know what it feels like.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.486
Maybe you felt like there was no one
you could talk to on an off day.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:59.636
You might've felt it when working remotely

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:01.666
or when you switched to a new team,